KZ3 patch 1064 (SPU pass 48): SPURS kernel lanes per dispatch follow the workload's ready count.
The kernel ran maxContention lanes (capped at the instance's nSpus) for every kicked dispatch; the ready count byte
only said "kicked". With the game's real HiPrio count of 5 (patch 1062, KZ3_SPURS_ATTR_SDK=1) that ran five
job-manager lanes per list and the menu hung (spu-48n2: the main thread parks on a list at 0x89E04 from t~140 s,
flips stop at 150 s). SPURS semantics: readyCount is the number of SPUs the workload asks for, up to maxContention.
KZ3_SPURS_LANES_READY=1 caps a kicked dispatch at the ready count read before the pass consumed one unit; always on:
a per-wid histogram of those ready counts and of the lanes run, in a [spurs-lanes] line every 10 s next to
[spurs-ready]. Default behaviour unchanged (opt-in until the A/B says otherwise).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.19.0 (SPU pass 154): three-way merge into the v0.19.0 chain, hunks kept as before, context follows v0.19 (chain glue, owner lane not re-reviewed).

